course: dictionary
lesson: 1691
title: The chrysalis
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chrysalis is the hard case a caterpillar makes around itself while it changes into a butterfly. Look at the words around it: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» The chrysalis comes after the caterpillar and before the butterfly, so it is the stage in the middle of the change.
explain: Inside the chrysalis, the caterpillar's body is broken down and rebuilt. «A caterpillar turns into a butterfly inside a chrysalis, where its body breaks down and is rebuilt.» Scientists call this big change complete metamorphosis, because the animal looks completely different at the end.
explain: Context can also show you a second meaning. «Alice tells it that one day it will turn into a chrysalis and then into a butterfly.» Here chrysalis is a time of quiet change before something new appears. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A chrysalis is the pupa stage of a butterfly's life cycle.
fact: The life cycle goes egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, then adult butterfly.
fact: The plural of chrysalis can be chrysalises or chrysalides.
fact: Phrases to know: inside the chrysalis, come out of the chrysalis, emerge from the chrysalis.
fact: In a figurative sense, a chrysalis is a time of quiet change before something new appears.
exercise: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» What comes after the caterpillar? | Adult moth | Egg | *Chrysalis | Leaf
exercise: What is a chrysalis? | *The hard case a caterpillar makes while it changes into a butterfly | The adult butterfly with its wings open | A wide river that butterflies cross | A type of leaf that caterpillars eat
exercise: «Inside the chrysalis its body is rebuilt into a butterfly with wings.» Find and copy the word that tells you the body is made again. | *rebuilt | wings | butterfly | body
test: Which order shows a butterfly's life cycle correctly? | Chrysalis, egg, adult butterfly, caterpillar | Egg, chrysalis, caterpillar, adult butterfly | *Egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, adult butterfly | Caterpillar, egg, adult butterfly, chrysalis
test: Sam says a chrysalis is a butterfly with wings. Is Sam right? | No, a chrysalis is a type of egg | Yes, it is the same as an adult butterfly | *No, a chrysalis is the hard case where the caterpillar changes into a butterfly | Yes, a chrysalis has wings that are folded up
exam: «Alice tells it that one day it will turn into a chrysalis and then into a butterfly.» What does chrysalis mean here? | A loud noise that frightens animals | A small green leaf on a tree | A type of fish that lives in ponds | *The hard case a caterpillar rests in while it turns into a butterfly
